# TFM Scrunch

Public two-page Next.js App Router microsite for the Sitecore + Scrunch stand at Technology for
Marketing 2026. No visitor login — the kiosk stays public. Audits are generated live by Gemini;
booth leads are written server-side to Firestore.

## Stack

- **Framework**: Next.js (App Router), React 19, Tailwind 4, `next/font/google` (Google Sans)
- **AI**: Gemini via `ai` + `@ai-sdk/google`, called only from `src/server/audit/` (server-only)
- **Persistence**: Firestore collections `tmf_scrunch_leads` and `tmf_scrunch_reports` (Firebase
  Admin, server-only) plus a local `data/leads.jsonl` fallback — see `src/server/audit/lead-log.ts`.
  No client Firebase SDK. PDFs are stored on the report document (`pdfBase64`).

## Conventions

- All visitor-facing branding/copy constants (company name, presenter, CTA label, event name,
  site URL) live in `src/lib/site-config.ts` — import `SITE` from there, never hardcode strings.
- Server-only AI code stays under `src/server/`, imported only from route handlers or other
  server-only modules — never from a `"use client"` component.
- Client components fetch via plain `fetch()` — there is no auth wrapper (`authFetch`) in this
  project, unlike the parent `SitecoreAiDemoSenario` repo it was forked from.
- Tables/report blocks reuse the same shared visual language as the parent repo's Scrunch
  workspace (rounded cards, `#8629ff` accent, `#17141f` dark panels) for a consistent brand feel.

## Docs

- README.md — overview, how to run locally, how the audit works
- AGENTS.md — paths and conventions for AI coding agents

## Deploy

Vercel (or similar): set `GEMINI_API_KEY` (required), `FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON` and
`NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID` (required to persist leads), `LEADS_ADMIN_SECRET` (stand desk),
`GEMINI_MODEL` (optional, defaults to `gemini-2.5-flash`), `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` (optional,
defaults to sitecore.com).
